    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **50 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and rewired household/duplicate logic accordingly.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** (the one create endpoint):\n- Now computes `householdId` for **every** owner up front as the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`, and always assigns it (so it feeds the identity key, household-size read-back, and duplicate detection).\n- **Household-duplicate detection** now keys off that computed `householdId`: if any existing owner already carries the same `householdId`, the create is a household duplicate and is **rejected with 409** \u2014 unless the request sets `sharesHousehold`, which now *only bypasses the block* (the link already exists by construction) and marks the owner a **declared household member**.\n- **Soft-match / `possibleDuplicate`**: a declared household member is never flagged (`possibleDuplicate=false`), since sharing a last name + postcode with an existing owner is now precisely what makes it a declared member rather than a suspected duplicate.\n\n**`generateHouseholdId`** \u2014 changed to key on `(lastName, postcode)` instead of `(lastName, address)`; removed the now-unused `findHouseholdMembers` and its backfill loop.\n\n**`DuplicateHouseholdException`** \u2014 updated constructor/message and javadoc to reflect the postcode-based household key (the 409 handler was already wired).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `sharesHousehold`, `householdId`, and `possibleDuplicate` descriptions to match the new behavior (documentation only; no field/shape changes).\n\nThe behavior change: two owners with the same last name and postcode are now the same household \u2014 the second is a 409 household duplicate unless it declares `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a member (sharing the same `householdId`) and not flagged as a possible duplicate. Identity-key collisions (same telephone/email/householdId) still 409 as before.",
